{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1786542920,"nonce":"BEFqzKdO4vZJfmQz90vBwISFCbM=","title":"Policy `reasons` uniqueness lives only in the DTO tag: the domain constructor and `policies_reasons_ck` both permit duplicates","was":"**What is wrong.** `notification_policies.reasons` is required to be a set, and exactly one of the three places CONTEXT.md §5b binds a rule to actually says so. The DTO `validate` tag carries `unique`; the domain constructor does not check it; the DDL `CHECK` does not check it. A duplicate reason is therefore storable by any writer that does not pass through `httpx.Bind` and the request DTO, and the contract declares that value impossible."}]}